Chromium 159.0.8154.6 -> 159.0.8154.8, for the 159.0.8154.6 tarball.

159.0.8154.8 is a tag on the 159 branch (refs/branch-heads/8154@{#231}) that
has no source tarball (as of 2026-11-13). It adds 141 branch commits to
159.0.8154.6 (#90), 73 of them not PGO/orderfile rolls, translation updates
or VERSION increments: security fixes (PDFium page unload re-entrancy, a
use-after-free in WidgetInputHandlerImpl::DispatchEvent, Oilpan notification
in HeapVector bulk operations, the Bluetooth chooser's event handler lifetime,
Contextual Tasks' async tasks; in the "Roll commits from side projects": V8's
regalloc spill slots and RegionAllocator size checks, Skia's vkWaitForFences
check, Dawn's wire null memoryHandle guard and six ANGLE GL/Vulkan/SPIR-V
fixes), Contextual Tasks, omnibox, OTP and New Tab Page changes, the New Tab
Page component extension's removal.

Generated from the upstream diffs between the tags: chromium/src
refs/tags/159.0.8154.6..159.0.8154.8 and the dependencies whose DEPS revision
changed (V8, Skia, Dawn, ANGLE), as served by Gitiles, with
scripts/chromium-delta.

Left out, as they cannot affect a Linux build: files not in the release
tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
translations (but en-GB), CI configuration, PGO/orderfile pointers, submodule
pointer updates, DEPS.

Added: the tarball's stamp files for the new commit (stamps.py:
build/util/LASTCHANGE{,.committime}, gpu/config/gpu_lists_version.h,
skia/ext/skia_commit_hash.h, gpu/webgpu/DAWN_VERSION and
gpu/webgpu/dawn_commit_hash.h; commit 8e9a74475caa6b98720c4c3872840ae06261a639,
refs/branch-heads/8154@{#231}). build/util/MINIBRANCH doesn't change.

Checked: applies to the 159.0.8154.6 tarball; chrome/VERSION becomes
159.0.8154.8; every patched source file is byte-identical to its version
at the tag (or its dependency's DEPS revision); it adds 2 files and deletes
7 (chrome/browser/resources/new_tab_page_extension/); the 159.0.8154.6
tarball's non-git files are all classified (tarball-generated.py with
generated.conf).

Apply with git apply.

